{"title":"Beat Reporter Roadmap","role":"Beat Reporter","summary":"A Beat Reporter is a journalist who specializes in consistently covering a particular subject, organization, industry, sport, team, institution, or geographic area. The reporter develops deep domain knowledge, maintains reliable sources, attends relevant events, verifies information, and produces timely news stories.","facts":{"Current degree":"BJMC / B.A. Journalism & Mass Communication","Course":"Sports / Business / Science Journalism"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Beat Reporter is a journalist who specializes in consistently covering a particular subject, organization, industry, sport, team, institution, or geographic area. The reporter develops deep domain knowledge, maintains reliable sources, attends relevant events, verifies information, and produces timely news stories."},{"type":"p","text":"For this pathway, the student can specialize in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sports Journalism — teams, athletes, tournaments, leagues, sports business"},{"text":"Business Journalism — companies, markets, startups, finance, industries"},{"text":"Science Journalism — research, technology, health science, climate, space"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The most valuable profile is not simply “good writer.” It is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Strong reporting","deep beat knowledge","source network","fact-checking","digital storytelling","data literacy"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Possible Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Journalism Intern, Reporting Intern, Junior Reporter, News Desk Assistant"}],[{"text":"1–3 Years"},{"text":"Beat Reporter, Staff Reporter, Digital Reporter"}],[{"text":"3–5 Years"},{"text":"Senior Reporter, Correspondent, Specialist Reporter"}],[{"text":"5–8 Years"},{"text":"Senior Correspondent, Bureau Reporter, Investigative Reporter"}],[{"text":"8–12 Years"},{"text":"Bureau Chief, Special Correspondent, Editor"}],[{"text":"Long Term"},{"text":"Executive Editor, Editorial Lead, Independent Journalist, Media Entrepreneur"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build During the Degree","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Journalism Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"News writing"},{"text":"News gathering"},{"text":"Journalism ethics"},{"text":"Media law"},{"text":"Interviewing"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Fact-checking"},{"text":"News judgment"},{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"Photography"},{"text":"Video journalism"},{"text":"Digital journalism"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the basic reporting formula:"},{"type":"flow","items":["News Tip","Research","Source Identification","Interview","Fact Verification","Story Writing","Editing","Publication","Follow-up"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Choose the Beat"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should start developing a specific domain specialization rather than remaining a general reporter."},{"type":"h","text":"Sports Journalism"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rules and formats"},{"text":"Teams and leagues"},{"text":"Player statistics"},{"text":"Sports business"},{"text":"Transfers"},{"text":"Contracts"},{"text":"Sports governance"},{"text":"Sports technology"},{"text":"Performance analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential beats:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cricket"},{"text":"Football"},{"text":"Olympics"},{"text":"Athletics"},{"text":"Esports"},{"text":"Sports business"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Business Journalism"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial statements"},{"text":"Corporate structures"},{"text":"Startups"},{"text":"Venture capital"},{"text":"Stock markets"},{"text":"Banking"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"M&A"},{"text":"Corporate governance"},{"te